      "persona": "Universal Persona Content",
      "author": "Dr. Mira Sen <mira.sen@asterlinktransit.com>",
      "subject": "Authorized scan window for Asterlink launch",
      "shortSummary": "Approved ranges, time window, and rules of engagement for the launch scan.",
      "date": "0001-01-01T00:00:00",
      "body": "{player},\n\nAsterlink Transit has approved a controlled scan window from 22:00 to 23:30 local time. The authorized IPv4 range is 10.42.18.0/24. The jump host is 10.42.18.10. Public DMZ services, ticketing validation, and vendor maintenance evidence may be reviewed only when the task instructions reference them.\n\nDo not scan 10.42.30.0/24, the broader vendor block, camera networks, or any external address unless written expansion is provided. Discovery and validation are allowed; exploitation, disruption, brute force, credential testing, and state-changing requests are prohibited.\n\nThe throughline is the undocumented host that appeared in the first handoff note: 10.42.18.73, also labeled ECHO-73. Treat it as a question, not a target to break.\n\nMira",
      "attachements": []
    }
  ]
}
